tion-agnostic stress</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-06-17-cow-w17/</link><pubDate>Wed, 17 Jun 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-06-17-cow-w17/</guid><description/></item><item><title>We speak ACR</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-06-03-cow-w15/</link><pubDate>Wed, 03 Jun 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-06-03-cow-w15/</guid><description/></item><item><title>We rise together</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-05-27-cow-w14/</link><pubDate>Wed, 27 May 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-05-27-cow-w14/</guid><description/></item><item><title>🤖 Will AI replace you? The uncomfortable truth about work</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/mind-infrastructure/2026-04-26-will-ai-replace-me/</link><pubDate>Sun, 26 Apr 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/mind-infrastructure/2026-04-26-will-ai-replace-me/</guid><description>&lt;h3 id="the-leverage-shift"&gt;The leverage shift&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The real risk is the colleague, vendor, or new hire who produces acceptable work &lt;strong&gt;faster and cheaper&lt;/strong&gt; by treating models as leverage while others defend process for its own sake.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What matters is &lt;strong&gt;comparative advantage&lt;/strong&gt; in a world where mechanical cognition is partially commoditized. Debating whether AI is &amp;ldquo;truly&amp;rdquo; thinking is a distraction from the immediate economic shift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="the-spell-check-mirror"&gt;The spell-check mirror&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The video uses spell-check as a historical mirror: it removed the prestige of memorizing exceptions and pushed the creative job up a layer. Ideas, structure, taste, and persuasion now matter more than catching every doubled letter.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>